; error: 7:9: 'add' changes 'xs', the copy this lambda keeps of a slice of the code around it, whose length only the slice itself changes; make the slice inside the lambda, or take it as a parameter, 'hold& xs'
; The copy a lambda keeps of a slice shares its items, not its length.
task main()
    region r
    hold xs = new [int]() at r
    hold f = [hold @r]() -> int
        xs.add(1)
        <- xs.len
    fi
    show(f())
fi
